  "*** THE RNG-STREAM SEARCH IS REFUTED AS A METHOD ***": {
    "what_was_tried": "both remaining questions — which template a room rolls, and which slots it fills — point at draws made at spawn time, and tools/rngstream.py makes the stream reconstructible backward from the live state. So: walk back 400 positions and test at each whether the next few draws select the observed slot subset without replacement, under any ordering.",
    "why_it_fails": "the hits are noise. Expected chance matches = positions * n! / (8*7*...), and the observed counts sit on that number. The spawn's position in the stream is unknown, the subsets are short, and every ordering counts — there is nothing left to discriminate with.",
